  "reason": "Evidence: config_021 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.629 acc / 0.599 F1 for only 4.54 GPU hrs, and it outperforms both the resnet50 variant (config_010, 0.619) and the scgpt variant (config_013, 0.518). The dominant design choices (multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool) are well-supported. The remaining untested dimension on this exact backbone is the fusion method: concat (tested) vs. weighted (untested). Question: Can learned weighted fusion between the RNA and image branches improve over simple concatenation, potentially closing the small accuracy gap or pushing past 0.63? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable change from the current best, so any accuracy shift is cleanly attributable to the fusion strategy. Expected cost is comparable to config_021 (~4–5 GPU hrs) since the architecture is identical. With 5 experiments remaining, this cheap, high-information exploitation step either yields a new best or confirms concat suffices, freeing later budget for larger structural changes (e.g., transformer aggregation or scvi_n200)."
